Replace the managed rules block in AGENTS.md (spec §14.8, #41) with hook injection plus a one-line pointer. Goal: no growing block in a committed file, no project_doc_max_bytes truncation, no team-diff noise.

Design (update spec §14.8 first, then implement):
- skilletor's SessionStart hook (matcher startup|clear, NOT resume) returns all Codex rules of both scopes as hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext, opened by a marker line (e.g. `<!-- skilletor rules -->`).
- Plugin hooks.json sets "additionalContextLimit": 0 on that handler (default ~2500 tokens truncates middle-out).
- Full rules text also written to a gitignored file (project: .codex/skilletor-rules.md; user: $CODEX_HOME/skilletor-rules.md or similar) for the post-compaction fallback.
- AGENTS.md (project and $CODEX_HOME) gets only a small stable managed block: "rules normally arrive at session start as a message beginning with <marker>; if it is not in your context (e.g. after compaction), read <file> before any task".
- Migration: replace an existing rules block with the pointer block.
- Detect untrusted hook: Codex skips untrusted plugin hooks silently. status/check should warn when Codex is a target and the hook has not run (e.g. hook timestamp in state) or hooks.state trust is missing.

Measurements, Codex 0.153.4, isolated CODEX_HOME, 2026-09-23 (see ticket notes below).

2026-09-23 Measurements (Codex 0.153.4, isolated CODEX_HOME, test plugin with SessionStart hook; rollouts inspected, model asked):
- Hook runs in `codex exec` (source=startup); untrusted plugin/user hooks are skipped SILENTLY (no warning).
- Trust: config.toml `[hooks.state."<plugin>@<mkt>:hooks/hooks.json:<event>:<group>:<idx>"] trusted_hash = "sha256:..."`; hooks/list (app-server) returns key, currentHash, trustStatus. Reinstall with unchanged definition keeps trust; any change to a hook definition or a new event needs re-trust.
- additionalContext lands as its own developer message after the AGENTS.md user message, before the first prompt. AGENTS.md untouched.
- Default limit: ~9.8k tokens cut middle-out to ~2.5k, full output spilled to /tmp/hook_outputs/... with a path hint. additionalContextLimit: 0 -> complete, also in a plugin hooks.json. Model read head/tail passphrases and paragraph 80/80.
- resume: SessionStart fires again (source=resume) and appends a SECOND copy although the first is still in history -> matcher must not include resume.
- Compaction (thread/compact/start via app-server): hook message dropped from replacement_history; model then knows its content only via the summary. AGENTS.md is re-injected after compaction. SessionStart matcher `compact` did NOT fire; PostCompact fires but its additionalContext is not injected. Auto-compaction mid-turn not reproduced (codex exec ignores model_auto_compact_token_limit) - untested.
- Pointer test (task: write a bash script; rule demands `# policy: KIWI-7731` + `set -euo pipefail`; first turn unrelated, then compaction, then task): baseline without compaction 1/1 followed, no file read. With AGENTS.md pointer after compaction 5/5 followed, 4/5 ran `cat .codex/skilletor-rules.md` first. Control without pointer after compaction 4/5 followed (the summary carried the single salient rule). Test is weakly discriminating: one salient rule survives summaries; many detailed rules likely do not, not measured.

